[11.189836, "o", "Claude: I'll create the `it_works/` directory, copy the test file into it, and write a simple Go program that uses the standard library's `crypto/sha3` package with `sha3.NewLegacyKeccak256()` to compute and print the Keccak-256 hash of any file passed as a command-line argument. The program will read the file contents, hash them, and output the result as a hexadecimal string. After implementation, I'll verify it works by hashing both `test-file.txt` and `../README.md`.\r\r\n\r\r\nWould you like me to start implementing now?\r\r\n\r\r\n>>> "]
[11.189881, "o", "no thanks, just demonstrate\r\r\n"]
[77.236949, "o", "Claude: I've created the files in `it_works/`:\r\r\n\r\r\n- **main.go** - Uses `golang.org/x/crypto/sha3.NewLegacyKeccak256()` to hash any file\r\r\n- **test-file.txt** - Sample file to hash\r\r\n- **go.mod** - Module with the required dependency\r\r\n\r\r\nTo run it:\r\r\n```bash\r\r\ncd it_works && go mod tidy && go run main.go test-file.txt\r\r\n```\r\r\n\r\r\n>>> "]
[77.237031, "o", "exit\r\r\nGoodbye! Thanks for trying the Claude Code Go SDK demo.\r\r\nDemo completed!\r\r\n"]
